WEBVTT

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.490
<i>Asu no egao no tame ni!
For the smiles of tomorrow!</i>

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.680
<i>Chikara to chikara butsukareba,,
When power collides with power,</i>

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.270
<i>arasoi wa hajimaru.
wars start.</i>

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.820
<i>Tatakau koto ga</i> yuuki <i>to</i>
I <i>don't think fighting</i>

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.820
<i>omowanai kedo...
equals bravery, but...</i>

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.220
<i>...mamoritai yo
...I want to protect</i>

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.780
kimi <i>no sono egao.
that smile on your face.</i>

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.400
<i>Asu e no geeto
We can't see the gate</i>

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.090
<i>mienai keredo....
to tomorrow, but...</i>

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.870
<i>dare ni</i> demo <i>aru yo.
one's inside each of us.</i>

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.530
<i>Let's open the gate!</i>

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:49.240
Kinou <i>no namida</i> wa
<i>The tears we shed yesterday</i>

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.510
<i>kitto muda ja nai.
are probably not in vain.</i>

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:55.880
<i>Arasoi no nai</i> mirai wa
<i>A future without war</i>

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.650
<i>ano tobira no mukougawa
waits behind that door.</i>

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.790
Mune <i>no oku</i> fukaku
<i>Retrieve the key lying</i>

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:06.730
<i>Jitto shimaikonda
deep inside your heart,</i>

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.530
<i>kagi wo takaku kakagete,
hold it up high,</i>

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:11.770
<i>fumidasou!
and step out!</i>

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:16.070
<i>Asu no egao no tame ni!
For the smiles of tomorrow!</i>

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:22.600
<i>You can open the gate!</i>

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.460
How about it, lkusawa?

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:51.840
I would like you to become a member
of our Political Thoughts Club.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:56.040
But this is so sudden...

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.670
It isn't sudden.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:02.710
I've been thinking of getting
you to join for some time now.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:06.490
Your clear head,
your superb character...

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.490
...and your perfect judgment.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:11.060
Any one of those
characteristics...

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.620
...is close to the ideal
high school students we hope to be.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.320
I'm not that great.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:20.330
What do you think?
Can I walk you to school?

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.070
There are some ideas from
our Political Thought Club...

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.770
...l wish to share with you.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.110
But I... Um, I...

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.480
Uh, I... have to wake up the
sleepyhead next door before I go!

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.520
So you like Ukiya more than me.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.060
WHAT?!

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:47.930
It was a joke. Still...

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.020
...l guess I've lost to Ukiya today.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.540
However, I will not
lose the next time.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:16.910
The ideal high school student, huh?

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.360
Hi, Rurippe!

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:32.200
What are you doing this early in
the morning, you gross, dirty pervert?!?

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.850
Oh, my. Kageyama gave you flowers?

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.860
Yeah. I don't know what to do.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.380
Hmph, you're lying.
You don't look displeased.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:57.820
Wow, who'd imagine giving flowers
for scouting people for your club?

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.770
That's Kageyama for you.

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:03.240
Oh, well. lf it were me,
I'd prefer to receive food.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.740
He's not inviting you, you know!

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:09.810
So this is what they mean by
"Cake before flowers."

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.680
Ayaya! Don't be such
a stranger, Captain.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:17.810
Just say the word, and
I'll make you Chinese food.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:21.910
Don't, Fei! Ukiya! If-
lf that's what you want...

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.520
...l'll make you a
packed lunch sometime!

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.930
Really? That would be great!

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.190
Right, I'll do my best!!

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.400
Ukiya!

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:41.240
Oh, my... Who is that?

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.870
I said get in!
What's your problem?!

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:45.540
What's going on?

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.580
Ms. Ochiai doesn't
seem to like him...

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.210
Do you suppose he's a villain?

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.840
All right, let's go help her!

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.720
Roger!

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:04.060
Oh, well. You'll be
my bride soon anyway.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.570
I'll get you nifty bridal wear
for the ceremony!

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.340
A pitch-black wedding dress!

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.320
Hey, you students!
Study like you're supposed to!

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.320
Find decent jobs, and then go on to
become the working ants of society...

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:28.220
...and that'll be the end of you!

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.660
W- Who the hell was that?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.460
Oh... ls everyone all right?

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:45.300
Who was that violent-
looking man? Do you know him?

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:48.740
Yes, um... He's my fiance.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.910
Oh, that explains it.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:53.240
So, he's your fiance...

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.040
WHAT??

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.950
You're getting married,
Ms. Ochiai?!

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.620
My, my! Congratulations!

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.660
Th- That's not what I meant!

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:10.130
Is that creep really the
man you're going to marry?!

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:12.930
MEDICAL ROOM

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:18.370
Well, my grandmother in my
hometown made the decision.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.470
I got a phone call last night,
and she said I'm too easy going...

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.570
...so I could use someone
who is a little aggressive.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.380
Maybe, but he's a
little too aggressive!

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.540
He is just a bully.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:33.080
And besides... what do you
think of him, Ms. Ochiai?

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:37.680
Are you going to get married just
like that on your grandmother's say-so?

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:42.990
Grandma believes that if you marry someone,
you will grow to see good things about them.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:46.760
I'm not talking about your grandmother!
What do YOU think of him?!

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:49.570
Who? Me?

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:52.440
You know! Don't you already
have your eye on somebody?!

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.410
I ' I-...

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.310
There's definitely someone!

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:00.370
Yes.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.350
But who do you suppose...

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.050
...this person could be?

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.090
Is it someone we know?

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.490
W- Well...

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:14.490
just a hint would be nice.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:18.760
I know! By chance, does
he happen to wear glasses?

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:21.700
What?! Um, yes.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:30.770
<i>Older woman ain't so bad, eitherl!</i>

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.780
H- Hold it! Princess Secretary!

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:41.720
Is he manly in both heart and body?!

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:43.920
What? Um, yes.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:47.430
ALL RIGHT!

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:51.060
A man's value is determined
by how manly they are!

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:53.100
So, how manly am I?!

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:03.400
At any rate, if you're in love with
someone else, you should confess your love!

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:07.440
That's right!
lkusawa is right!

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:13.390
As for me...

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.220
...Ukiya is...

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.380
Me?

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:21.260
Ukiya is THE ONE I LOVE!!!

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.500
Eek! I said it!

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:29.940
See? You tell yours,
too, Ms. Ochai!

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:33.510
You have to clear your own way
to your own future!

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.580
Isn't that right, lkusawa?

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:39.270
Huh? Uh, y- yes...

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:48.340
<i>Oh, boy, oh, boy...
Ruri broke it!</i>

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.220
<i>Ooh, don? blame me, Ruri.</i>

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.850
<i>Go and apologize, Ruri.</i>

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:56.520
<i>But I, uh...</i>

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.970
<i>It's Miracle Mask to the rescuel!</i>

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.710
It's Miracle Mask to the rescue...

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:21.880
At any rate, if you're in love with someone else,
you should confess your love!

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.320
Confess your love, huh?

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:33.530
Quick, let's go!

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:37.540
I'm starving! Guess I'll
eat cafeteria food today.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:41.130
Or maybe I'll get buns.
What do yon think, Bancho?

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:43.180
How about both?

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.610
U- Uh, Ukiya?

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:50.380
Ukiya!

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:56.850
Ukiya, I made you a lunch!
Please eat it!

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.890
For me?
That's right!

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:03.190
Thanks, Kaoru.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:07.630
WHY?! How come Ukiya gets all
the attention?! It's unfair!

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.100
You're lucky, Ukiya!

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.660
You playboy!

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.710
You get all the chicks!

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:14.710
Guess I'll dig in!

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.670
That's a luxurious lunch.

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:22.610
You think so?

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.210
What do you think, Ukiya?

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.910
Mm, it's good! It's real good!

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:30.180
Thank goodness!

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:33.630
By the way, Kaoru, how
did you hurt your hands?

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:37.650
Oh, it's nothing. I fell
down the stairs a second ago.

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:44.370
Oh, yeah. Rurippe, didn't you
want to see me about something?

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:47.410
Huh? Uh, it- it's nothing.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:50.970
Well, I have student
council work to do.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.910
That reminds me! Ukiya, did you hear?

00:10:56.980 --> 00:11:01.480
Ms. Ochiai is going back to her hometown
this Saturday on the noon express.

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:03.750
Saturday?!

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:05.450
That's tomorrow!

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:17.600
'Got it!

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:20.770
Humph. What's with him,
drooling all over her.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:25.770
I'll never make him a lunch again,
even if he does ask me to.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:28.710
That jerk.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.850
It's good.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:37.650
Kageyama...

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:43.260
Uh, excuse me! Still, it looks like you're
good at homemaking as well as studying.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.700
Th- Thank you.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:50.570
Oh, yeah! Tomorrow, Saturday afternoon,
our Political Thought Club...

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:55.630
...is having a meeting in Yoyogi Park.
Won't you please come?

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:56.730
Tomorrow?

00:11:56.810 --> 00:11:58.400
Is it inconvenient?

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:00.450
N- No.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.680
That's Ukiya and...

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:10.620
Maybe they're going into
the gym equipment storage room.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:13.660
Come to think ofit,
I've heard of some students...

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.790
...using the storage room
for shameless deeds.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:18.560
Shameless deeds?

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:22.230
Well, I'm sure it has
nothing to do with those two.

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:31.200
What have we here?

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:32.940
Are you all right, Kaoru?

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:38.010
I'm sorry. I got up so early to
make the lunch, I feel a little dizzy.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:39.390
Got up early?

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:44.720
Uh, no... More important, are
you really sure you want to help?

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:47.160
Of course, to thank
you for the lunch.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:50.360
Let's see... You need the mat
and the vaulting boxes, right?

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:51.520
Yes!

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.690
They make a pretty good couple.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:56.370
I... I'm sorry.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:02.970
Ikusawa! Don't forget!

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:06.240
Tomorrow afternoon in Yoyogi Park!

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.860
Excuse me for being late, Commander.

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:20.690
Yes...

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.460
Where is Agent lkusawa?

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:27.690
I think she went home
right after school today.

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:32.840
Oh,well.This time, our
information is still unverified.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:36.070
I will contact her once
we have final confirmation.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:38.570
Useless.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.210
Now, about the paranormal
frequency picked up...

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:45.010
...by the Far Eastern branch
surveillance network yesterday...

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:47.810
I never!

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:03.800
<i>I'm sorry, Rurippe.</i>

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.270
<i>Actually, l...</i>

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.720
What do you want to do today?
Want to go see a movie?

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:27.450
Do we have muscle
training again today?

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:29.050
Say! Hey, Rurippe.

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:31.860
<i>Rurmppe!</i>

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:34.870
I keep telling you not
to call me Rurippe!

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:40.340
Sorry! Anyway, today's the day
Ms. Ochiai is going home...

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:44.110
You're coming with us, right?

00:14:44.180 --> 00:14:45.800
Oh, yeah.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.810
Kaoru is waiting for us.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:48.870
Kaoru is coming, too?

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:52.410
C'mon, let's hurry! Bancho is
already on his way ahead of us.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:55.980
I'm not going!
What?

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:58.530
I'm not going. I have
something else to do!

00:14:58.590 --> 00:14:59.860
Something else?

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:01.900
Ikusawa!

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:05.390
Bye.
Wh- Hey!

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:07.700
Let's go, Kageyama.

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:11.730
Wait, Rurippe! Are you sure that's
what you want to do, Rurippe?!

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.540
Never call me that again!

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.710
Whoa.

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:27.410
Move it, move it, move it!
Damn, you're slow! Get in the train!

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:28.580
Get in!!

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:31.590
E- Excuse me, but aren't
we taking the express?

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.960
You're slow, so you'll be more
comfortable on the slow train.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:35.890
But my work...

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:40.920
I'm being generous enough to take
a slow woman like you to be my wife...

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.900
...so be grateful!

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:48.030
Today's meeting marks a new
first step in our club activities.

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:51.080
I'm pleased you decided to join us.

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:52.940
Th- Thanks.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:56.380
<i>I'm not talking about your grandmother!
What do YOU think of him?</i>

00:15:56.450 --> 00:16:00.410
<i>At any rate, if you're in love with
someone else, you should confess your love!</i>

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:05.350
<i>Ukiya is the one I love!!</i>

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:09.320
<i>See? You tell yours,
too, Ms. Ochai!</i>

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.060
<i>You have to clear your own way
to your own future!</i>

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:18.960
lkusawa?

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:23.000
I'm sorry. I... I...

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:26.470
I have something
important to do! So l can't!

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:37.660
<i>Ueno, this is Ueno. All passengers,
please clear the doors for incoming passengers.</i>

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:40.660
It's no good. I can't
spot her anywhere.

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:42.700
No luck here, either.

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:47.690
I'm sure she said
the express leaving at 1:22...

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.070
Hmm...

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:50.600
What now, Ukiya?

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.000
At any rate, let's split up
and look for her.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:57.170
Even if she won't change her mind,
we should at least see her off.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:58.870
NO!!

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:03.840
We can't watch her go!
She loves someone else...

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:06.940
...so how can she get
married to some nobody?!

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:09.150
I can't... I won't...

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:11.550
I won't stand for it!!

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:21.560
Move it, move it, move it!

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:24.640
Buy our train lunches
after we're on the train.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:27.070
And naturally, you're buying.

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.370
Right.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.770
Ms. Ochiai!

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:31.070
Ikusawa?!

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:34.050
You can't, Ms. Ochiai!
You can't go!

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.050
Who is this brat?!

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:39.550
If you love someone else, you
can't go away without telling him!

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:42.650
If you love him,you have
to tell him you love him!

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:48.060
Get lost! She's going
to be my wife!

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.530
I'm going to marry her,
and I will own her!

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:53.160
That's horrible!! just because
you get married to someone...

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:55.400
...it doesn't mean they
become your possession!

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:57.100
Shut up!

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:02.170
Stop it!

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:18.720
What's this?!

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:20.120
Paranormal frequencies registered!

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:22.160
Y- You mean...?!

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:29.400
What?!

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:43.180
Piece of shit!

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:53.330
Marriage!

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:55.760
An invader!
Ms. Ochiai!

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.920
For the time being, we
should get out of here!

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:00.900
Yes, this is Ukiya!

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:03.130
What?! Paranormal frequencies
at the train station?!

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:04.760
What?!

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:06.830
Please stand back, Ms. Ochiai!

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.380
R' Right!

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.180
That won't be necessary, Rurippe!

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:20.380
You're all here!

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.110
You, too, Commander?!

00:19:22.190 --> 00:19:25.180
All civilians have already
been evacuated from the station!

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:28.830
To defeat the invader
in the guise of a fiance!

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:31.160
To defend the peace
of Ueno Station!

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:34.030
Head out, Gate Keepersfl

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.030
Roger, AEGIS!

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:38.430
He's here!

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:41.170
Enemy confirmed.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.780
GATE OPEN!

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:50.750
Ultra Cyclone Chop!

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:59.850
Kaoru Kick!!

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:05.450
Bewitching Melody!

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:09.100
Iron Wall!

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:12.860
Explosive Panda Fire Ball!

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:15.370
Inner Circle Throwl!

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:35.360
You are an excellent secretary.
You are my right arm.

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:37.900
Please don't say you're going home.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.660
Yes, sir.

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:44.260
Um, C- Commander...

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:45.240
What is it?

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:48.610
Um, thank you.

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.270
Yes...

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:10.990
lf you love someone, tell them,
huh? Yeah. That's true.

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:16.560
After all, I'm runny-nosed
fidgety little Rurippe no longer!

00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:18.100
<i>Okay“</i>

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.640
Good morning, little birds!

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:26.640
Hi, Rurippe.

00:21:30.020 --> 00:21:34.980
IDIOT!

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:10.910
<i>Itsumademo wasurenai
We received many things</i>

00:22:11.090 --> 00:22:14.960
<i>takusan no mono moratta ne.
we will never forget.</i>

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:19.930
<i>Sora no iro utsushite hikaru
I don't mean the blue jewels flashing</i>

00:22:20.470 --> 00:22:23.300
<i>aoi houseki ya
with colors of the sky...</i>

00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:25.440
koinu-tachi
or a big yard

00:22:25.440 --> 00:22:30.610
<i>hanemawaru hiroi</i> niwaja <i>nai,
with puppies romping around,</i>

00:22:30.610 --> 00:22:33.950
motto motto daijina
but something <i>much</i> more

00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:38.580
<i>mono wo.
important.</i>

00:22:39.290 --> 00:22:43.450
<i>Kinou Kara kyou e
From yesterday to today,</i>

00:22:43.520 --> 00:22:48.080
<i>kyou kara asu e to
from today to tomorrow,</i>

00:22:48.560 --> 00:22:54.860
boku-tachi wa aruite yuku yo.
we will walk toward the future.
